** SPOILERS **

First off, unlike with my mage Slash'EM ascension, I didn't make any
modifications to the Monk starting code, and I didn't re-role when I
got bad starting stats; I started with average stats an inventory.

Things went normally for me until I accidentally killed my dog, Spot,
by displacing him into a pit I'd dug; uh-oh.  Fortunately, he'd stolen
a little-dog figurine from a tools shop in the mall one level above,
so I soon had Killer to act as a cursed-item detector.  I cleared out
Sokoban, got a BoH, and went down in the normal dungeons until I found
a co-aligned alter; then I sac'd until I got rid of my god's anger,
and then sac'd more until I got the Gauntlets of Defense.  With the
half-physical damage they provided, I cleared out the Gnomish Mines
rather easily, and got a Magic Candle from the Mine's lighting shop;
somewhere along the way, I got Telepathy by praying.  Oh, and a the
vampires in the catacombs mine's end level provided my with [CoMR, so
I had a replacement for when one of them got burned; that was really
nice.

I went down through the Dungeons of Doom, passing by the Quest but
stopping to get the Key of Neutrality and to rob the Black Market
(didn't get anything real special from the market, mainly just
identify and remove curse scrolls).  I wanted to get to XL 16 so I
could kill Vecna and get his hand before doing the Quest.  I found
speed boots in the Spider Caves, and then I got really lucky at the
Guild of Disgruntled Adventurer's: got an athame for quick engraving,
plus a (0:1) wand of wishing.  I wished for 2 blessed ?oCharging (got
one), recharged, then wished for a "oReflection, 2 blessed ?oGenocide,
and a blessed magic marker.  Kept on going until I hit XL 16,
level-teleported back up to the top of the dungeons, maxed out
divine-protection with the mine-town priest, and then went to kill
Vecna.

Once I got his hand for providing 1/2 physical damage, I replaced my
Gauntlets of Defense with Gauntlets of Power by wresting one final
wish out of the /oWishing.  I then went on the Quest, and finished of
Kaen real easily with the aid of a !oParalysis.

So back down I go, and find *another* pre-Castle /oWishing in the
Temple of Moloch; yipee!  Some more magic markers, and my AC is
getting pretty low; by the time I get to the Castle, it's down to -51.
Medusa and the Castle were easy (the Hand of Vecna and two blessed
healthstones makes me regen *very* quickly), and I never even used the
Castle /oWhishing.  The hardest part of Gehennom was Demogorgon, not
because of the illness (which was no problem with my blessed +6
unicorn horn), but because of the psi-bolts ("Your head suddenly aches
very painfully!"); those do a *lot* of damage.  All of the other demon
lords weren't that bad, and Yeenoghu was especially easy (as always;
seems he'd only be a problem for someone who hadn't gotten reflection
by that point).

Vlad was really easy, since I engraved "Elbereth" a bunch of times
while he was sleeping/meditating, and then just pounded him
bare-handed while he was was scared, but unable to flee.  Down, down I
go, clearing out Frankenstein's lab, just to have cleared out as many
special branch-levels as possible (except for the Orc Caverns, since
one of the orcs had a /oDraining).  Found the vibrating square, go
back to the Wizards Tower, then kill Rodney by crashing a !oParalysis
on his head (while wearing a =oFreeAction) and then pounding on him
bare-handed.  Level-teleport down to the Vibrating Square, kill Rodney
with a /oDeath, and clear out the sanctum with the aid of a
=oConflict.

Going back up was boring, except for one place where it seemed that
the amulet's Mysterious Force was in action, even though it's supposed
to be gone in Slash'EM; turned out there was a hole with some items on
top of it one step before the up-stair case of one level, and I wasn't
paying enough attention to the messages (d'oh!).

When I got to the planes, I tried to use a glass orb to find the
portals, like I did with my Mage ascensions, but the my exploded on
my.  I thought "that's strange", wished for a new one, found the
portal out of the Plane of Earth, and then my second orb exploded on
me in the Plane of Fire.  I'd forgotten that orbs don't work so well
for low intelligence characters, and I still only had an Int of 10.
D'oh!  I tried find the Fire portal using the Amulet, but finally got
fed up, wrote out a ?oGoldDetection with my last ?oBlankPaper, and
used that to find the portal.  Used the Amulet to find the portal on
the Plane of Water, then used my =oConflict to get through the Astral
plane, rather than wishing for a cockatrice corpse, like I have on my
previous ascensions.  I went left, killed Pestilence with my bare
hands, and found the right altar immediately.

When I sac'd, it gave me the option to sac the Hand of Vecna, and I
tried it, just to see what would happen; it was accepted, even though
it's the mummified hand of an evil lich.  Then I sac'd the amulet.

